# Copy to agents/estate.env and edit. KEY=VALUE, no spaces around "=".

# AGENTS_REPO is NOT set here. The kit's SETUP.md puts it in Claude Code's settings ("env"); or set it
# in your shell profile to this repo's absolute path (export AGENTS_REPO=/path/to/your/repo). Hooks
# fall back to the session's project folder when it is unset; bin/drift and
# bin/note-to-overmind exit with an error if it is unset.

# Optional secret-manager CLI (H2). Empty = H2 is off.
# Set to the command name if you use one (the hook then refuses bare "list everything" calls that
# would print secret values). Examples: op (1Password), pass, gopass, rbw. Suggested default: leave
# it empty if you only use a browser or phone password manager; there is no command to guard.
SECRET_CLI=

# Role notes: hooks treat a session as unattended (H4 blocks instead of asking) when AGENT_ROLE is set in
# its environment. Leave AGENT_ROLE unset for your own interactive sessions: there the owner's-hand actions
# raise a permission prompt and your answer is the go. AGENT_ROLE also names the carry file a session
# reads at start (agents/state/carry/<role>.md; unset = overlord).
#   AGENT_ROLE=overlord | worker | verifier | ...   (set by whoever launches a headless run)
#   AGENT_INITIATIVE=<id>                            (optional; tags drift and notes lines)
